  "label": "TMUA 2023 · Paper 1 · Question 9",
  "lead": "<img class=\"source-question\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"button\" aria-label=\"Enlarge question\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"TMUA 2023 · Paper 1 · Question 9 — Count solutions of (1+3cos3θ)²=4 on 0°≤θ≤180°.\">",
  "options": [
    "A",
    "B",
    "C",
    "D",
    "E",
    "F"
  ],
  "correct": "E",
  "hints": [
    {
      "title": "Keep both square-root branches",
      "body": "<p>The equation gives <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>&#x0002B;</mo><mn>3</mn><mi>cos</mi><mn>3</mn><mi>&#x003B8;</mi><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></math> or <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>&#x0002B;</mo><mn>3</mn><mi>cos</mi><mn>3</mn><mi>&#x003B8;</mi><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mo>&#x02212;</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></math>.</p>",
      "recap": "There are two different cosine levels to count.",
      "pitfall": "Taking only the positive square root loses valid solutions.",
      "pause": "Rearrange each branch to an equation for <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mi>cos</mi><mn>3</mn><mi>&#x003B8;</mi></mrow></math>.",
      "recall": [
        {
          "lessonId": "p1-b1-l16",
          "reminder": "Solving a squared equation requires both signs unless a separate restriction removes one."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Scale the angle interval",
      "body": "<p>Let <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mi>φ</mi><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mn>3</mn><mi>&#x003B8;</mi></mrow></math>. Then <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><msup><mn>0</mn><mrow><mo>&#x02218;</mo></mrow></msup><mo>&#x02264;</mo><mi>φ</mi><mo>&#x02264;</mo><msup><mn>540</mn><mrow><mo>&#x02218;</mo></mrow></msup></mrow></math>, and the two equations are <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mi>cos</mi><mi>φ</mi><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow></mfrac></mrow></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mi>cos</mi><mi>φ</mi><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mo>&#x02212;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></math>.</p>",
      "recap": "The new interval spans one and a half turns.",
      "pitfall": "Using the original <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><msup><mn>180</mn><mrow><mo>&#x02218;</mo></mrow></msup></mrow></math> interval for φ undercounts roots.",
      "pause": "Sketch cosine through <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><msup><mn>0</mn><mrow><mo>&#x02218;</mo></mrow></msup><mo>&#x0002C;</mo><mtext>&#x000A0;</mtext><msup><mn>180</mn><mrow><mo>&#x02218;</mo></mrow></msup><mo>&#x0002C;</mo><mtext>&#x000A0;</mtext><msup><mn>360</mn><mrow><mo>&#x02218;</mo></mrow></msup></mrow></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><msup><mn>540</mn><mrow><mo>&#x02218;</mo></mrow></msup></mrow></math>.",
      "recall": [
        {
          "lessonId": "p1-b1-l15",
          "reminder": "Multiplying an angle scales its allowed interval before solution counting."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Add distinct branch counts",
      "body": "<p>Count each cosine level separately on the expanded angle interval. Use one complete turn plus the remaining half-turn, checking the closed endpoint. The two different levels cannot share an input.</p>",
      "recap": "The two levels cannot share a solution.",
      "pitfall": "The endpoint <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><msup><mn>540</mn><mrow><mo>&#x02218;</mo></mrow></msup></mrow></math> is included.",
      "pause": "Find both branch counts and add them; scaling the angle back does not change the number of inputs.",
      "recall": [
        {
          "lessonId": "p1-b2-l04",
          "reminder": "Count each trigonometric branch and check closed endpoints before combining."
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "solution": "<p>Taking both square-root branches gives <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mi>cos</mi><mn>3</mn><mi>&#x003B8;</mi><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow></mfrac></mrow></math> or <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mi>cos</mi><mn>3</mn><mi>&#x003B8;</mi><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mo>&#x02212;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></math>. With <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mi>φ</mi><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mn>3</mn><mi>&#x003B8;</mi></mrow></math>, the interval becomes <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><msup><mn>0</mn><mrow><mo>&#x02218;</mo></mrow></msup><mo>&#x02264;</mo><mi>φ</mi><mo>&#x02264;</mo><msup><mn>540</mn><mrow><mo>&#x02218;</mo></mrow></msup></mrow></math>.</p><p>The first equation has three solutions: one in each of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00028;</mo><msup><mn>0</mn><mrow><mo>&#x02218;</mo></mrow></msup><mo>&#x0002C;</mo><mtext>&#x000A0;</mtext><msup><mn>90</mn><mrow><mo>&#x02218;</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00029;</mo><mo>&#x0002C;</mo><mtext>&#x000A0;</mtext><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00028;</mo><msup><mn>270</mn><mrow><mo>&#x02218;</mo></mrow></msup><mo>&#x0002C;</mo><mtext>&#x000A0;</mtext><msup><mn>360</mn><mrow><mo>&#x02218;</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00029;</mo><mo>&#x0002C;</mo><mtext>&#x000A0;</mtext><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00028;</mo><msup><mn>360</mn><mrow><mo>&#x02218;</mo></mrow></msup><mo>&#x0002C;</mo><mtext>&#x000A0;</mtext><msup><mn>450</mn><mrow><mo>&#x02218;</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00029;</mo></mrow></math>. The second has two, at <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><msup><mn>180</mn><mrow><mo>&#x02218;</mo></mrow></msup></mrow></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><msup><mn>540</mn><mrow><mo>&#x02218;</mo></mrow></msup></mrow></math>. Their sets are disjoint, and each φ gives one <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mi>&#x003B8;</mi></mrow></math>.</p><p><strong>Answer E: 5 solutions.</strong></p>",
